# virtualenv + caches
software/.venv/
# training-only venv: torch 2.2.2 + numpy<2, kept SEPARATE because this Intel Mac tops out at
# torch 2.2.2 (no cp39 x86_64 wheel above it) and that build predates numpy 2 — torch.from_numpy
# raises "Numpy is not available" against the main venv's numpy 2.0.2. Runtime stays numpy-only:
# train here, export .npz weights, run the forward pass in numpy. Disposable; recreate with
#   python3 -m venv software/.venv-train && pip install "numpy<2" torch
software/.venv-train/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
nohup.out

